# Scenario for scripts/record-scenario.py: the 68000 mandelbrot on the
# MC68010P12 on the MC68000P board at 10 MHz. MULS multiplies two words
# into a long word and DIVS divides that long word by a word; the 16-bit
# bus fetches a word at a time.
#
# ADDRESS IS PINNED TO THE CURRENT samples/mc68000/mandelbrot.s19: the
# MOVE.W of vB at 4CA, before the MULS of B*B. If mandelbrot.asm/.inc or
# the .s19 ever change, re-check it against the fresh .lst before
# recording -- a stale address will look like it works (it disassembles
# *something*) while showing the wrong thing.

key ?
pace 2.0

key R
upload samples/mc68000/mandelbrot.s19

# Reset again so SSP and PC come from the uploaded reset vector.
key R
pace 1.5

# Stop at the MOVE.W of vB: D0 gets B.
type g
wait Go until?
command 4CA 4
pace 2.0

# MULS B*B, MOVE.W vA, MULS A*A, SUB, EXT.L, then DIVS by F.
step 7
pace 1.5

# Watch one frame render.
run 1 300
